# Web3Forms access key for the contact form.
# Get a free key at https://web3forms.com/ (it is emailed to you after verification).
# The key decides which inbox receives the messages.
#
# Local:  copy this file to `.env` and fill in the key below.
# Vercel: Project Settings -> Environment Variables -> add the same key, then redeploy.
#         Vite bakes env values into the client bundle at build time, so redeploy
#         is required whenever the key changes.
#
# Note: Vite only exposes `VITE_*` variables to client-side code via import.meta.env.
# If you set this in Vercel as `WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY`, Vite won't see it unless the
# variable is named `VITE_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY` — or set both with the same value.
VITE_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=
WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=
